# Upload code (excludes .venv, .venv-desktop-build, build/, dist/):
#   ./scripts/ec2_upload.sh ubuntu@ec2-xx.ap-southeast-1.compute.amazonaws.com
# Copy secrets only:
#   scp -i ./video-transcripts-server.pem .env ubuntu@<host>:~/youtube-transcripts-scrape/.env
# rsync -e must be "ssh -i KEY.pem", not "-e ./KEY.pem"
#
# Loaded by download_channel_transcripts.py: `.env` next to this script, then cwd `.env`
# (cwd overrides). You can copy or symlink vars from kyle-insta-video-transcripts/.env;
# only the variables below are read by this script (Instagram-only keys are ignored).

# --- Webshare rotating residential (recommended on EC2 / datacenter IPs) ---
# Dashboard: https://dashboard.webshare.io/proxy/settings (Residential plan)
# WEBSHARE_PROXY_USERNAME=your_proxy_username
# WEBSHARE_PROXY_PASSWORD=your_proxy_password
# Legacy aliases also accepted: WEBSHARE_USER, WEBSHARE_PASSWORD

# --- Or a single HTTP(S) proxy for transcript requests (not used with Webshare above) ---
# Same URL for http and https, e.g. Webshare static/datacenter style:
# TRANSCRIPT_PROXY=http://user:pass@p.webshare.io:80/

# --- Optional Simplepush (IP-ban stop + run-complete notification) ---
# SIMPLEPUSH_KEY=your_key
# Alternate env name supported by the script: 56F6LP=your_key
# Title/event are CLI only: --simplepush-title, --simplepush-event

# Not read by this script (safe if present from a shared .env):
# TRANSCRIPT_NO_PROXY, WEBSHARE_PROXY_HOST, WEBSHARE_PROXY_PORT, DIRECT_INSTAGRAM_DOWNLOADS, …
